Open a pull request for the current branch with `gh`.

Context for the description, if provided: $ARGUMENTS

- Commit any remaining work first (see the commit skill). If on `main` or `master`, stop and tell the user.
- Check for an existing PR with `gh pr view`. If one exists, update it rather than opening a second.
- Push the branch with `git push -u origin HEAD`. Never force push.
- Title: conventional commit style, lowercase, prefixed with `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, etc.
- Reference other PRs by full URL (e.g. `https://github.com/org/repo/pull/54`), never `#54`.
- Do not add attribution trailers or session links (no `Co-Authored-By:`, no `Claude-Session:`, no claude.ai/code URLs).
- Write the description kindly and clearly for the human reviewers. Favor separate paragraphs, headers, and readability.
- Follow the repo's PR guidance or `pull_request.md` template if one exists. Otherwise use this format:

```
# Goal
*The high-level goal of this PR. What problem does it solve, or what functionality does it add?*

# Summary
*Summarize the change, linking each commit with a one-line summary.*
[abcdef](link-to-commit) - added migration to drop users table

# Testing
*Is this change tested within this PR? Was test coverage added? Does it need post-change verification instead?*
```
